branch: feature/intent-taxon-wired-to-tiers
worktree: ../okay-wt-wired

why: The third and last of the frictions the first caller exposed, and
  the consumer's request 1 read literally. What landed as `Taxon` is
  one taxonomy that NEITHER trained tier reads: every `train` infers
  its classes from whatever labels its rows happen to carry, and a
  caller checks `taxon.has` by hand afterwards. A tier should be
  fittable AGAINST a taxonomy, and a `Trained` should carry the
  taxonomy it was fitted to, so a disagreement is an error at fit time
  rather than a wrong class at answer time.

